<title>USA: Storm threat to shipping in Caribbean - WSC.</title>
<headline>Storm threat to shipping in Caribbean - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Storm Marco was drifting eastward in the western Caribbean about 340 miles south-southwest of Kingston, Jamaica, independent forecaster Weather Services Corp said.</p>
<p>Marco will become an increasing risk to shipping as winds approach 70 mph in 24 to 48 hours, and was expected to track across Jamaica and far eastern Cuba late in this period.</p>
<p>Heavy rains could lead to flooding in these areas during that time and also across the island of Hispaniola.</p>
</text>
